  BEFORE: The period's change less the five-year average change of the same period
  AFTER:  The mean of the values 52, 104, 156, 208 and 260 weeks before (for a monthly series, the same month of the five years before), with their lowest and highest on hover; given only when all five are held. It stands for normal at this point of the year only for a series with a season and no trend. For production, which has grown, and for positioning, it measures the five years' trend, not the season; and where a series changed its level within the five years (New York's and SPP's oil burned for power fell to near zero from 2023), it stands for a level the series no longer has. Read the year before
  BEFORE: The last 52 values held: 52 weeks for a weekly series, 52 months (over four years) for a monthly one. A week or month not held is left out and the line closes over it, so a line can span more than 52 steps; each point's 
